{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Fortigi/PSMutant/v0.5.0/schemas/v1/config.schema.json",
  "_comment": "Mutation testing for OmadaWeb.PS. The policy keys are edited by hand; mutate, tests and _untested are generated by ./Build/Update-MutationConfig.ps1 -Update and verified on every pull request by -Check. Run: ./Build/build.ps1 -Task Mutate (whole tree, weekly) or -Task MutateChanged (pull request).",
  "_sandboxSubtreesComment": "The tests import the SOURCE module (their default -ModulePath is OmadaWeb.PS/OmadaWeb.PS.psm1, which dot-sources Public/ and Private/), so a mutant spliced into a source file inside the sandbox is what they load. Build/ is copied because some covered tests read the build scripts and the dependency manifests.",
  "sandboxSubtrees": [
    "OmadaWeb.PS",
    "Tests",
    "Build"
  ],
  "_workersComment": "1, deliberately. Workers are runspaces in ONE process, and three suites share process-wide state: StrictMode.Tests.ps1 writes $Env:OMADAWEBPS_STRICTMODE, Install-EdgeDriver.Tests.ps1 writes $Env:TEMP and $Env:TMP, and the integration tests bind a fixed port (Start-WebServer.ps1, 9080). In parallel those race and show up as KILLED mutants, inflating the score. Raise this only after those suites are isolated.",
  "workers": 1,
  "operators": [
    "BinaryOperator",
    "BooleanLiteral",
    "NumberLiteral",
    "NegationRemoval"
  ],
  "coveredLinesOnly": true,
  "timeoutFactor": 4,
  "timeoutFloorSeconds": 30,
  "_thresholdsComment": "break is the floor both the weekly whole-tree run and the pull request run on changed files are held to; only ever raise it. 75 comes from the first measurement (issue #91): 78.8% (430/546) over the 60 source files whose covering tests could run outside Windows. Recalibrate it from the first weekly run, which measures all mapped files on Windows.",
  "thresholds": {
    "high": 85,
    "low": 70,
    "break": 75
  },
  "reportPath": "buildoutput/mutation/ps-mutation.json",
